Send a message again when its connection drops, instead of failing it.

While a sandbox starts, the server holds the message's POST open until the
agent can take it, and a phone can lose that connection: Tailscale on iOS
reapplies its routes when the session's Pod joins the tailnet. The server
still delivered the message, but the send failed with "Load failed", put
the message back in the composer and showed an error.

postEvent now sends a message with a stable_id again, unchanged, when fetch
fails without a response (a TypeError), after 1, 2, 4 and 8 seconds and then
every 15 seconds, about two minutes in all. The server
(0017-resend-dropped-message.patch) delivers it once, so a resend waits for
the first copy or gets its answer. Other events, HTTP errors and aborts
fail as before. When every resend fails, the error says the message may not
have been sent and that sending it again won't send it twice.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0023-sandbox-picker-under-composer.patch.

